course: dictionary
lesson: 1018
title: A tree kept small
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A new word often shows its meaning in the words around it. Read the sentence and ask what the clues tell you. «Bonsai are ordinary trees kept small by careful cutting of roots and branches in small pots.» The words kept small and careful cutting are the clues: a bonsai is a normal tree that someone has made small on purpose.
explain: The sentence also tells you what a bonsai is not: «not special tiny kinds». So a bonsai is not a special sort of tree that stays small by nature. Any ordinary tree can become a bonsai when it is grown in a shallow pot and trimmed with care.
explain: Bonsai is also an art, and the sentence shows it is patient work. «Some bonsai are hundreds of years old.» Those words tell you that the care is slow and steady, and that a tree can be looked after for a very long time.
fact: A bonsai is a tree or shrub kept very small by growing it in a shallow pot.
fact: Bonsai is also the art of growing such trees, which comes from Japan and, before that, China.
fact: Careful cutting of roots and branches keeps a bonsai small.
fact: Bonsai trees are normal kinds, such as maple, pine and juniper.
fact: Some bonsai are hundreds of years old and can be passed down in families.
exercise: «Bonsai are ordinary trees kept small by careful cutting.» What does kept small tell you about a bonsai? | *It is an ordinary tree made small on purpose | It grows very fast in the wild | It can only grow in water | It is a special tiny kind of tree
exercise: Which plant could be grown as a bonsai? | A tiny wild plant that never gets bigger | *A pine grown in a shallow pot and carefully trimmed | A giant oak growing wild in a forest | A rose in a field that is never cut
exercise: Bonsai, the art, first came from which countries? | Italy and France | Brazil and Kenya | *Japan and China
test: What is a bonsai? | A plant that lives only in water | A type of flower | A special tiny species of tree | *An ordinary tree kept very small in a shallow pot
test: Which are normal kinds of tree used for bonsai? | Sun, moon and stars | Dragon, unicorn and phoenix | *Maple, pine and juniper | Cheese, bread and jam
exam: Using the sentence «Bonsai are ordinary trees kept small by careful cutting of roots and branches», what can you tell about bonsai? | *They are ordinary trees made small with care | They never live longer than a year | They must be grown from seeds in the sea | They are a special tiny species
